custom_link = "https://www.britishmuseum.org/collection/object/A_1979-0305-0-48-4"
blurb = "This example page is from a travel guide of the Tōkaidō (Eastern Sea Road), connecting Edo (present-day Tōkyō) to Kyōto, the most important of the Five Routes of the Edo period.

Such guides were targeted as much towards travelers as towards common people who wanted to experience travel vicariously. The print depicts villages, shrines, and famous locations, and includes text that lists things such as travel fees and restaurant recommendations.

Follow the link above to view more pages from this travel guide."
